      {
        "id": 208979,
        "name": "Phantom5613",
        "username": "Phantom5613",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/{size}/1906_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-11-20T23:21:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"X-metal\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/x-metal/48/4892_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> X-metal:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;X-metal wrote:<br><blockquote>i doubt it's an April fools joke. Adam and Christopher's humor isn't that good. After all, they mostly rely on the same \"and then they died\" joke for their humor. And also their \"other podcast\" jokes.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nI don't know, their one April Fools joke was pretty good.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/content/major-announcement\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/content/major-announcement</a>\n</blockquote></div>\ni would watch that, but only if they were drawn the regular way. Legacy looks weird. And the art in general looks like something out of a crappy Saturday morning cartoon without &nbsp;a plot. Granted, it does prove that Adam can draw anything.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>T'was the joke, me thinks.</p>",
